          "responseMode": "text",
          "expected": [
            "{{k}}"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "solutionReview": {
        "headline": "A vertical shift moves the horizontal asymptote.",
        "reasoning": [
          "The parent exponential approaches $y=0$, but adding {{k}} shifts every output and the asymptote vertically.",
          "The actual asymptote is $y={{k}}$, while the y-intercept is {{y0}}."
        ],
        "answerSummary": "y-intercept {{y0}}; asymptote $y={{k}}$."
      },
      "attemptFeedback": [
        "Separate the initial value from the horizontal asymptote; they are not generally the same feature."
      ],
      "supportHints": [
        "In $a(b)^x+k$, the asymptote is shifted from 0 to k."
